  "description": "George Lucas was paid $150,000 to write and direct Star Wars, kept the merchandising and sequel rights, and sold Lucasfilm to Disney in 2012 for $4.05 billion.\n\nSources:\n- Wikipedia: George Lucas: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/George_Lucas\n- Wikipedia: Star Wars (film): https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Star_Wars_(film)\n- Wikipedia: Lucasfilm: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lucasfilm\n\nFrom the cited pages: a July 13, 1973 deal memo gave Lucas $150,000 to write and direct; after American Graffiti's success he declined to renegotiate a higher fee, instead gaining ownership of licensing and merchandising rights (novelizations, clothing, toys) and sequel rights; Star Wars released in 1977; on October 30, 2012 Disney acquired Lucasfilm for $4.05 billion, about half cash and half Disney shares. Not financial advice.\n\n#shorts #georgelucas #starwars #howtheymakemoney",
